My single most effective filter is dropping posts to 4+ groups
everywhere.  I also have more restrictive numbers on a few high noise
groups.

I filter out everyone from webtv but not from googlegroups.  Part of the
reason is I posted through google when I travelled for work and kept at
it for a while after settling down.  Part of the reason is the fact that
it is in the top 10 posting sources.  Dropping every google poster
because there are a lot of google spammers to me throws out the baby
with the bath water.

With google the choice is simple - See and ignore all of the spam and
worse all of the abusers, or switch away from google.  There exists
software to filter out by poster when using google - That can drop
abusers but it can not drop spammers.

I use eternal-september.org most of the time.  Very good spam filtering.
I use XPN because it was easy to install and it has good filtering
options.

!kill Xpost %>3
!kill From "webtv.net"
!kill Xref "misc.misc"

A few sample lines from my filter file.


